    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by the explosive 82.13 score for **Pete Crow-Armstrong**. Facing a favorable matchup against Lowder (4.77 xERA), **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from a massive 10% boost for hitting in the leadoff spot and a 14% platoon advantage, but his true value lies in the \"slow delivery\" factor\u2014with a 100% stolen base opportunity rating, he is our premier weapon for the scarcest category in 5x5. Complementing him are **Yordan Alvarez** (66.16) and **Junior Caminero** (64.76), both of whom offer elite high-floor production. **Yordan Alvarez** remains a cornerstone despite a slight park penalty, as his xwOBA of .454 provides an anchor for our counting stats. **Lars Nootbaar** also earns a strong recommendation (63.92) as his lead-off spot against Tidwell offers a perfect storm of positive platoon and order adjustments.\n\nThe decision-making process for the utility slots was particularly tight, with **Carson Benge** (55.59) serving as the most difficult omission. While **Carson Benge** boasts a solid profile against the right-handed Brown, his overall efficiency projection fell just shy of the active roster\u2019s cluster of players like **Christian Yelich** and **Kyle Schwarber**, who benefit more significantly from their established lineup positions today. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler** (48.39) closely; while he earns a start, he faces a daunting matchup against the elite Skubal (2.74 xERA). While **Dillon Dingler** receives a \"slow pitcher\" bump that keeps his SB potential active, his scoring is heavily suppressed by the SP skill disadvantage. Owners should note that **Gary Sanchez** is excluded today due to non-availability, and we continue to bench **Caleb Durbin** and **Hector Rodriguez**, as their current splits and bottom-of-the-order assignments do not provide enough leverage against their respective opposing arms to justify burning a game cap.",
